Web API Summary (Interview Revision)
What is a Web API?

A Web API (Application Programming Interface) is a service that allows different applications to communicate over HTTP.

It acts as a middle layer between the client and the database.

Architecture:

Client (MVC / React / Angular / Windows Forms / Mobile)
                    |
                 HTTP Request
                    |
                 Web API
                    |
             Business Logic
                    |
                 Database
Why do we use Web API?
Share data between multiple applications.
Separate UI from business logic.
Improve security.
Return data in JSON or XML.
Support CRUD operations.
Enable communication through HTTP.
HTTP Methods
Method	Purpose
GET	Retrieve data
POST	Insert new data
PUT	Update existing data
DELETE	Delete data
PATCH	Partial update

Example:

GET /api/employees

Returns all employees.

